 "ごつい": "صُلْب (Solid and firm.) / صَعْب (Having a severe property; presenting difficulty.) / لَا يُدْحَضُ (Unquestionable; unequivocal.)  [hard]\nごっつい is more emphatic / رَيْفِيّ, قَرَوِيّ (Country-styled or pastoral; rural.)  [rustic] / الْأُقْصَى, الْأَبْعَد (Of a place, the most remote, farthest or outermost.) / شَدِيد (In the greatest or highest degree; intense.) / غَيْر اِعْتِيَادِيّ (Excessive, or far beyond the norm.) / خَطِير (Drastic, or of great severity.) / مُتَطَرِّف (Of sports, difficult or dangerous; performed in a hazardous environment.) / أَخِير (Ultimate, final or last.)  [extreme]",
